WEBVTT

00:00:00.419 --> 00:00:01.960
A human analyst has to listen

00:00:01.839 --> 00:00:03.719
to the business question like, which

00:00:03.599 --> 00:00:05.260
stores are at risk and then

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.580
mentally translate that subjective

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.840
human anxiety into a series of

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.239
complex database joins?

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.379
They have to know all the

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.139
quirks of the system.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.019
Exactly. They have to know that

00:00:14.899 --> 00:00:16.560
the warehouse table uses an underscore

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.240
in the column name while the

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.660
sales table uses camel case.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.620
They have to know which filters

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.100
to apply and which departmental definition

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.380
to enforce. The obvious vulnerability

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.360
there that if that specific human

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.580
goes on vacation or you know

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.600
quits. The institutional knowledge

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.820
of how to ask the database

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.359
a question just walks right out

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:35.980
the door with them.
